{"name":"Sauvignon","hex":"#f4eae4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sauvignon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several grape varieties and associated wines originally from France"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sauvignon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sauvignon blanc","blocks":[{"text":"Sauvignon blanc is a green-skinned grape variety that most likely originated in the Loire Valley wine region in France, though it has also been historically cultivated in Bordeaux. The grape most likely gets its name from the French words sauvage (\"wild\") and blanc (\"white\") due to its early origins as an indigenous grape in South West France. It is possibly a descendant of Savagnin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Sauvignon_blanc_grapes.jpg/330px-Sauvignon_blanc_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauvignon_blanc"},{"title":"Sauvignonasse","blocks":[{"text":"Sauvignonasse is a white wine grape of the species Vitis vinifera prevalent in the Italian region of Friuli, and adjacent territories of Slovenia. It is widely planted in Chile, where it was historically mistaken for Sauvignon blanc."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/VIVC12543_FRIULANO_Cluster_in_the_field_17025.jpg/330px-VIVC12543_FRIULANO_Cluster_in_the_field_17025.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauvignonasse"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Parts_of_the_original_Cresta_blanca_winery_at_Wente.jpg/500px-Parts_of_the_original_Cresta_blanca_winery_at_Wente.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Parts_of_the_original_Cresta_blanca_winery_at_Wente.jpg/1280px-Parts_of_the_original_Cresta_blanca_winery_at